WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.211
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.511 --> 00:00:08.503
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:15.275
Unit two: Personality and Character. In this unit, you will describe personality in detail.

4
00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:17.470
self-confident.

5
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.064
self-confident means sure of your own abilities.

6
00:00:21.364 --> 00:00:23.712
She's self-confident without being arrogant.

7
00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:27.284
Your turn. Say: self-confident.

8
00:00:29.984 --> 00:00:31.160
self-confident.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.198
short-tempered.

10
00:00:33.898 --> 00:00:36.443
short-tempered means getting angry very quickly.

11
00:00:36.743 --> 00:00:38.963
My old boss was very short-tempered.

12
00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:41.967
Your turn. Say: short-tempered.

13
00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:45.796
short-tempered.

14
00:00:46.783 --> 00:00:47.692
level-headed.

15
00:00:48.392 --> 00:00:52.864
level-headed means calm and sensible, especially in difficult situations.

16
00:00:53.164 --> 00:00:55.570
We need someone level-headed to lead the project.

17
00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.748
Your turn. Say: level-headed.

18
00:01:01.448 --> 00:01:02.728
level-headed.

19
00:01:03.717 --> 00:01:04.706
narrow-minded.

20
00:01:05.406 --> 00:01:09.345
narrow-minded means not willing to accept new ideas or other opinions.

21
00:01:09.645 --> 00:01:12.317
It's narrow-minded to judge people by where they come from.

22
00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:15.623
Your turn. Say: narrow-minded.

23
00:01:18.323 --> 00:01:19.499
narrow-minded.

24
00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:21.345
big-hearted.

25
00:01:22.045 --> 00:01:24.474
big-hearted means very kind and generous.

26
00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:27.737
Our big-hearted neighbour cooks for elderly people.

27
00:01:28.437 --> 00:01:31.043
Your turn. Say: big-hearted.

28
00:01:33.743 --> 00:01:34.756
big-hearted.

29
00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:36.647
quick-witted.

30
00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:40.496
quick-witted means able to think and answer quickly and cleverly.

31
00:01:40.796 --> 00:01:43.376
The quick-witted student always had a funny reply.

32
00:01:44.076 --> 00:01:46.147
Your turn. Say: quick-witted.

33
00:01:48.847 --> 00:01:49.802
quick-witted.

34
00:01:50.817 --> 00:01:51.829
thick-skinned.

35
00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:55.702
thick-skinned means not easily upset by criticism.

36
00:01:56.002 --> 00:01:58.082
Journalists need to be thick-skinned.

37
00:01:58.782 --> 00:02:01.017
Your turn. Say: thick-skinned.

38
00:02:03.717 --> 00:02:04.753
thick-skinned.

39
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:06.763
laid-back.

40
00:02:07.463 --> 00:02:10.229
laid-back means relaxed and not worried about things.

41
00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:14.374
My brother is so laid-back that nothing stresses him.

42
00:02:15.074 --> 00:02:17.854
Your turn. Say: laid-back.

43
00:02:20.554 --> 00:02:21.532
laid-back.

44
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:24.539
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:24.839 --> 00:02:26.804
How would you describe a good team leader?

46
00:02:28.117 --> 00:02:31.614
Someone level-headed and self-confident, but never short-tempered.

47
00:02:32.917 --> 00:02:36.231
My manager is very laid-back. Is that a problem?

48
00:02:37.517 --> 00:02:40.854
Not if she's well-organised too. Is she open to new ideas?

49
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.812
Yes, she's the opposite of narrow-minded. And she's big-hearted.

50
00:02:47.117 --> 00:02:49.720
She sounds like a wonderful person to work for!

51
00:02:51.017 --> 00:02:54.154
Grammar focus: Compound adjectives.

52
00:02:54.454 --> 00:02:58.671
Compound adjectives are made of two words, usually joined with a hyphen.

53
00:02:58.971 --> 00:03:03.072
For example: big-hearted, short-tempered and well-organised.

54
00:03:03.372 --> 00:03:05.778
With numbers, we don't add s: a two-hour meeting.

55
00:03:06.078 --> 00:03:11.862
Use a hyphen in compound adjectives before a noun, and don't add -s to numbers: a ten-minute break.

56
00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.897
Now read and listen. Can Personality Change?.

57
00:03:16.197 --> 00:03:20.693
For many years, psychologists believed that personality was fixed by the age of thirty.

58
00:03:21.983 --> 00:03:26.386
However, recent studies suggest that our character continues to develop throughout life.

59
00:03:27.683 --> 00:03:31.842
A short-tempered teenager can become a level-headed adult with experience.

60
00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.402
Even shy people can become more self-confident by practising new behaviours.

61
00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:41.935
In other words, who we are is partly a choice we make every day.

62
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.717
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:48.945
Calm and sensible in difficult situations is blank.

64
00:03:49.245 --> 00:03:52.852
A, level-headed. B, short-tempered. C, narrow-minded.

65
00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.791
The answer is A: level-headed.

66
00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:01.633
It was a blank journey.

67
00:04:01.933 --> 00:04:06.016
A, six-hours. B, six-hour. C, six hours.

68
00:04:10.017 --> 00:04:11.947
The answer is B: six-hour.

69
00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:16.146
Not easily upset by criticism means blank.

70
00:04:16.446 --> 00:04:20.343
A, thick-skinned. B, laid-back. C, big-hearted.

71
00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.152
The answer is A: thick-skinned.

72
00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:30.918
She is a blank manager. Everything is planned perfectly.

73
00:04:31.218 --> 00:04:35.498
A, well-organised. B, organise-well. C, well organising.

74
00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:41.320
The answer is A: well-organised.

75
00:04:42.817 --> 00:04:45.443
According to the text, personality blank.

76
00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:50.813
A, is fixed by thirty. B, continues to develop. C, never changes.

77
00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:56.990
The answer is B: continues to develop.

78
00:04:58.483 --> 00:05:02.912
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe the personality of someone you admire.

79
00:05:08.212 --> 00:05:15.044
My grandmother is big-hearted and level-headed. She's never short-tempered, even in difficult situations.

80
00:05:15.344 --> 00:05:16.949
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.810
Great work today! You learned eight new words and compound adjectives.

82
00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.737
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

83
00:05:26.037 --> 00:05:28.353
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

84
00:05:28.653 --> 00:05:31.700
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

